        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "The Other Side of Zero"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.121,
            0.617,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": "You must travel 4 steps. That is why 5 + 4 = 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.152,
            0.819,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "(Remember: **Starting Number + Movement = Target Number**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.181,
            0.692,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": "The corresponding subtraction statement is 9 – 5 = 4."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.212,
            0.833,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "(Remember: **Target Number – Starting Number = Movement needed**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.272,
            0.833,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": "Now, from 9, if you wish to go to 3, how much must you travel along the number line?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.318,
            0.836,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.384,
            0.832,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": "You must move 6 steps backward, i.e., you must move –6. Hence, we write 9 + (–6) = 3."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.437,
            0.833,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": "(Remember again : **Starting Number + Movement = Target Number**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.489,
            0.705,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "The corresponding subtraction statement is 3–9=–6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.52,
            0.833,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": "(Remember again: **Target Number – Starting Number = Movement needed**)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.579,
            0.804,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": "Now, from 3, if you wish to go to – 2, how far must you travel?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.61,
            0.837,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_11_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.673,
            0.831,
            0.718
          ],
          "content": "You must travel –5 steps, i.e., 5 steps backward. Thus, 3+(–5)=–2. The corresponding subtraction statement is: –2 –3=–5."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.736,
            0.301,
            0.759
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.549,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
